#: src/authentication.md:3
msgid "Authenticate with Zed"
msgstr ""

#: src/authentication.md:5
msgid ""
"Signing in to Zed is not required. You can use most features you'd expect in "
"a code editor without ever doing so. We'll outline the few features that do "
"require signing in, and how to do so, here."
msgstr ""

#: src/authentication.md:7
msgid "What Features Require Signing In?"
msgstr ""

#: src/authentication.md:9
msgid "All real-time [collaboration features](./collaboration/overview.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/authentication.md:10
msgid ""
"[LLM-powered features](./ai/overview.md), if you are using Zed as the "
"provider of your LLM models. To use AI without signing in, you can [bring "
"and configure your own API keys](./ai/llm-providers.md#use-your-own-keys)."
msgstr ""

#: src/authentication.md:12
msgid "Signing In"
msgstr ""

#: src/authentication.md:14
msgid ""
"Zed uses GitHub's OAuth flow to authenticate users, requiring only the `read:"
"user` GitHub scope, which grants read-only access to your GitHub profile "
"information."
msgstr ""

#: src/authentication.md:16
msgid ""
"Open Zed and click the `Sign In` button in the top-right corner of the "
"window, or run the `client: sign in` command from the command palette (`cmd-"
"shift-p` on macOS or `ctrl-shift-p` on Windows/Linux)."
msgstr ""

#: src/authentication.md:17
msgid "Your default web browser will open to the Zed sign-in page."
msgstr ""

#: src/authentication.md:18
msgid "Authenticate with your GitHub account when prompted."
msgstr ""

#: src/authentication.md:19
msgid ""
"After successful authentication, your browser will display a confirmation, "
"and you'll be automatically signed in to Zed."
msgstr ""

#: src/authentication.md:21
msgid ""
"**Note**: If you're behind a corporate firewall, ensure that connections to "
"`zed.dev` and `collab.zed.dev` are allowed."
msgstr ""

#: src/authentication.md:23
msgid "Signing Out"
msgstr "登出"

#: src/authentication.md:25
msgid "To sign out of Zed, you can use either of these methods:"
msgstr ""

#: src/authentication.md:27
msgid ""
"Click on the profile icon in the upper right corner and select `Sign Out` "
"from the dropdown menu."
msgstr ""

#: src/authentication.md:28
msgid "Open the command palette and run the `client: sign out` command."
msgstr ""

#: src/authentication.md:30
msgid "Email Addresses"
msgstr "電子郵件地址"

#: src/authentication.md:32
msgid ""
"Your Zed account's email address is the address provided by GitHub OAuth. If "
"you have a public email address then it will be used, otherwise your primary "
"GitHub email address will be used. Changes to your email address on GitHub "
"can be synced to your Zed account by [signing in to zed.dev](https://zed.dev/"
"sign_in)."
msgstr ""

#: src/authentication.md:34
msgid ""
"Stripe is used for billing, and will use your Zed account's email address "
"when starting a subscription. Changes to your Zed account email address do "
"not currently update the email address used in Stripe. See [Updating Billing "
"Information](./ai/billing.md#updating-billing-info) for how to change this "
"email address."
msgstr ""

#: src/authentication.md:36
msgid "Hiding Sign In button from the interface"
msgstr ""

#: src/authentication.md:38
msgid ""
"In case the Sign In feature is not used, it's possible to hide that from the "
"interface by using `show_sign_in` settings property. Refer to [Visual "
"Customization page](./visual-customization.md) for more details."
msgstr ""

