#: src/ai/mcp.md:143
msgid ""
"Zed's Agent Panel provides the `agent.tool_permissions.default` setting to "
"control tool approval behavior for the native Zed agent:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:145
msgid ""
"`\"confirm\"` (default) — Prompts for approval before running any tool "
"action, including MCP tool calls"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:149
msgid ""
"For granular control over specific MCP tools, you can configure per-tool "
"permission rules. MCP tools use the key format `mcp:<server>:<tool_name>` — "
"for example, `mcp:github:create_issue`. The `default` key on a per-tool "
"entry is the primary mechanism for MCP tools, since pattern-based rules "
"match against an empty string for MCP tools and most patterns won't match."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:157
msgid ""
"MCP servers configured in Zed are forwarded to [external agents](./external-"
"agents.md) via the [Agent Client Protocol](https://agentclientprotocol."
"com/). External agents can also access MCP servers from their own native "
"configuration files."
