msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:163
msgid ""
"When a MCP server encounters an error while processing a tool call, the "
"agent receives the error message directly and the operation fails. Common "
"error scenarios include:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:166
msgid "Invalid parameters passed to the tool"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:167
msgid "Server-side failures (database connection issues, rate limits)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:168
msgid "Unsupported operations or missing resources"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/mcp.md:170
msgid ""
"The error message from the context server will be shown in the agent's "
"response, allowing you to diagnose and correct the issue. Check the context "
"server's logs or documentation for details about specific error codes."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:3
msgid "AI"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:5
msgid ""
"Zed is an open-source AI code editor. AI runs throughout the editing "
"experience: agents that read and write your code, inline transformations, "
"code completions on every keystroke, and conversations with models in any "
"buffer."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:7
msgid "How Zed approaches AI"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:9
msgid ""
"Zed's AI features run inside a native, GPU-accelerated application built in "
"Rust. There is no Electron layer between you and the model output."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:11
msgid ""
"**Open source.** The editor and all AI features are [open source](https://"
"github.com/zed-industries/zed). You can read how AI is implemented, how data "
"flows to providers, and how tool calls execute."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:12
msgid ""
"**Multi-model.** Use Zed's hosted models or [bring your own API keys](./llm-"
"providers.md) from Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, Ollama, and 8+ other "
"providers. Run local models, connect to cloud APIs, or mix both. Switch "
"models per task."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:13
msgid ""
"**External agents.** Run Claude Agent, Gemini CLI, Codex, and other CLI-"
"based agents directly in Zed through the [Agent Client Protocol](https://zed."
"dev/acp). See [External Agents](./external-agents.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:14
msgid ""
"**Privacy by default.** AI data sharing is opt-in. When you use your own API "
"keys, Zed maintains zero-data retention agreements with providers. See "
"[Privacy and Security](./privacy-and-security.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:16
msgid "Agentic editing"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:18
msgid ""
"The [Threads Sidebar](./parallel-agents.md#threads-sidebar) is where you "
"organize agent work. Start a thread, give it a task, and the agent reads, "
"edits, and runs code in your project. You can run multiple threads at once, "
"each using a different agent and working against different projects. See "
"[Tools](./tools.md) for the capabilities available to Zed's built-in agent."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:20
msgid ""
"The [Agent Panel](./agent-panel.md) is the conversation view for the active "
"thread. Use it to send prompts, review changes, add context, and interact "
"with the agent as it works."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:22
msgid ""
"You can extend agents with additional tools through [MCP servers](./mcp.md), "
"control what they can access with [tool permissions](./tool-permissions.md), "
"and shape their behavior with [rules](./rules.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:24
msgid ""
"The [Inline Assistant](./inline-assistant.md) works differently: select code "
"or a terminal command, describe what you want, and the model rewrites the "
"selection in place. It works with multiple cursors."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:26
msgid "Code completions"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:28
msgid ""
"[Edit Prediction](./edit-prediction.md) provides AI code completions on "
"every keystroke. Each keypress sends a request to the prediction provider, "
"which returns single or multi-line suggestions you accept with `tab`."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:30
msgid ""
"The default provider is Zeta, Zed's open-source model trained on open data. "
"You can also use GitHub Copilot, or Codestral."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:32
msgid "Getting started"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:34
msgid ""
"[Configuration](./configuration.md): Connect to Anthropic, OpenAI, Ollama, "
"Google AI, or other LLM providers."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:35
msgid ""
"[Parallel Agents](./parallel-agents.md): Run multiple threads at once with "
"the Threads Sidebar."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:36
msgid ""
"[External Agents](./external-agents.md): Run Claude Agent, Codex, Aider, or "
"other external agents inside Zed."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:37
msgid "[Subscription](./subscription.md): Zed's hosted models and billing."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:38
msgid ""
"[Privacy and Security](./privacy-and-security.md): How Zed handles data when "
"using AI features."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/overview.md:40
msgid ""
"New to Zed? Start with [Getting Started](../getting-started.md), then come "
"back here to set up AI. For a higher-level overview, see [zed.dev/ai]"
"(https://zed.dev/ai)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:3
msgid "Parallel Agents"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:5
msgid ""
"Parallel Agents lets you run multiple agent threads at once, each working "
"independently with its own agent, context window, and conversation history. "
"The Threads Sidebar is where you start, manage, and switch between them."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:7
msgid ""
"Open the Threads Sidebar with <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-alt-j\\|ctrl-alt-"
"j</kbd>."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:9
msgid ""
"**Note:** From version 0.233.0 onward, the Agent Panel and Threads Sidebar "
"are on the left by default. The Project Panel, Git Panel, and other panels "
"move to the right, keeping the thread list and conversation next to each "
"other. To rearrange panels, right-click any panel icon."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:11
msgid "Threads Sidebar"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:13
msgid ""
"The sidebar shows your threads grouped by project. Each project gets its own "
"section with a header. Threads appear below with their title, status "
"indicator, and which agent is running them. Threads running in linked Git "
"worktrees appear under the same project as their main worktree. See "
"[Worktree Isolation](#worktree-isolation)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:15
msgid ""
"To focus the sidebar without toggling it, use <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-"
"alt-;\\|ctrl-alt-;</kbd>. To search your threads, press <kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-f\\|ctrl-f</kbd> while the sidebar is focused."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:17
msgid "Switching Threads"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:19
msgid ""
"Click any thread in the sidebar to switch to it. The Agent Panel updates to "
"show that thread's conversation."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:21
msgid ""
"For quick switching without opening the sidebar, use the thread switcher: "
"press <kbd class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-tab\\|ctrl-tab</kbd> to cycle forward "
"through recent threads, or hold `Shift` while pressing that binding to go "
"backward. This works from both the Agent Panel and the Threads Sidebar."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:23
msgid "Thread History"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:25
msgid ""
"To remove a thread from the sidebar, you can archive it by hovering over it "
"and clicking the archive icon that appears. You can also select a thread and "
"press <kbd class=\"keybinding\">shift-backspace\\|shift-backspace</kbd>. "
"Running threads cannot be moved to history until they finish."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:27
msgid ""
"The Thread History view holds all your threads, including ones that you have "
"archived. Toggle it with <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-g\\|ctrl-g</kbd> or "
"by clicking the clock icon in the sidebar bottom bar, next to the sidebar "
"toggle."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:29
msgid ""
"To restore a thread, open Thread History and click the thread you want to "
"bring back. Zed moves it back to the thread list and opens it in the Agent "
"Panel. If the thread was running in a Git worktree that was removed, Zed "
"restores the worktree automatically."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:31
msgid ""
"To permanently delete a thread, open Thread History, hover over the thread, "
"and click the trash icon. This removes the thread's conversation history and "
"cleans up any associated worktree data. Deleted threads cannot be recovered."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:33
msgid ""
"You can search your threads in history; search will fuzzy match on thread "
"titles."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:35
msgid "Importing External Agent Threads"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:37
msgid ""
"If you have external agents installed, Zed will detect whether you have "
"existing threads and invite you to import them into Zed. Once you open "
"Thread History, you'll find an import icon button in the Thread History "
"toolbar that lets you import threads at any time. Clicking on it opens a "
"modal where you can select the agents whose threads you want to import."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:39
msgid ""
"**Note:** Thread import is subject to agent support. Some agents (such as "
"Cursor and Gemini CLI) are not currently supported."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:41
msgid "Running Multiple Threads"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:43
msgid ""
"Each thread runs independently, so you can send a prompt, open a second "
"thread, and give it a different task while the first continues working. To "
"scope a new thread to a specific project, hover over that project's header "
"in the Threads Sidebar and click the `+` button, or use <code "
"class=\"hljs\">agents sidebar: new thread in group</code> from the keyboard. "
"See [Creating New Threads](./agent-panel.md#new-thread) for the other entry "
"points."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:45
msgid ""
"Each thread can use a different agent, so you can run Zed's built-in agent "
"in one thread and an [external agent](./external-agents.md) like Claude Code "
"or Codex in another."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:47
msgid "Multiple Projects"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:49
msgid ""
"The Threads Sidebar can hold multiple projects at once. Each project gets "
"its own group with its own threads and conversation history."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:51
msgid ""
"To add another project to the sidebar, click the **Add Project** button "
"(open-folder icon) in the sidebar bottom bar. The popover that opens lists "
"your recent projects and also provides **Add Local Folders** and **Add "
"Remote Folder** buttons at the bottom."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:53
msgid "Multi-Root Folder Projects"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:55
msgid ""
"A single project can contain multiple folders (a multi-root folder project). "
"Agents can then read and write across all of those folders in a single "
"thread. There are multiple ways to set one up:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:57
msgid ""
"**From the sidebar:** Click the **Add Project** button, choose **Add Local "
"Folders**, and select multiple folders in the file picker. They open "
"together as one multi-root project."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:58
msgid ""
"**From the title bar:** Click the project picker (the leftmost project "
"name). For any local entry in the recent projects list, hover it and click "
"the folder-with-plus icon (**Add Folder to this Project**) to merge that "
"project's folders into the current project."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:59
msgid ""
"**From the Project panel:** Right-click a root folder or any empty space in "
"the Project panel and choose **Add Folders to Project** to add more folders "
"to the current project."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:61
msgid "Worktree Isolation"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:63
msgid ""
"If two threads might edit the same files, start one in a new Git worktree to "
"give it an isolated checkout."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:65
msgid ""
"Worktrees are managed from the title bar. Click the worktree picker (to the "
"right of the project picker) to switch between existing worktrees or create "
"a new one. New worktrees are created in a detached HEAD state, so you won't "
"accidentally share a branch between worktrees."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:67
msgid ""
"Once you're in a new worktree, use the branch picker next to the worktree "
"picker to create a new branch or check out an existing one. If the branch "
"you pick is already checked out in another worktree, the current worktree "
"stays in detached HEAD until you choose a different branch."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:69
msgid ""
"To automate setup steps whenever a new worktree is created use a [Task hook]"
"(../tasks.md#hooks). The `create_worktree` hook runs automatically after Zed "
"creates a linked worktree, with `ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT` pointing at the new "
"worktree and `ZED_MAIN_GIT_WORKTREE` pointing at the original repository."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:71
msgid ""
"After the agent finishes, review the diff and merge the changes through your "
"normal Git workflow. If the thread was running in a linked worktree and no "
"other active threads use it, moving the thread to Thread History saves the "
"worktree's Git state and removes it from disk. Restoring the thread from "
"history restores the worktree."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:73
msgid "See Also"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:75
msgid ""
"[Agent Panel](./agent-panel.md): Manage individual threads and configure the "
"agent"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:76
msgid ""
"[External Agents](./external-agents.md): Use Claude Code, Gemini CLI, and "
"other agents"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/parallel-agents.md:77
msgid "[Tools](./tools.md): Built-in tools available in each thread"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:3 src/ai/rules.md:55
msgid "Using Rules"
msgstr "使用規則"

#: src/ai/rules.md:5
msgid ""
"Rules are prompts that can be inserted either automatically at the beginning "
"of each [Agent Panel](./agent-panel.md) interaction, through `.rules` files "
"available in your project's file tree, or on-demand, through @-mentioning, "
"via the Rules Library."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:7
msgid "`.rules` files"
msgstr "`.rules` 檔案"

#: src/ai/rules.md:9
msgid ""
"Zed supports including `.rules` files at the root of a project's file tree, "
"and they act as project-level instructions that are auto-included in all of "
"your interactions with the Agent Panel."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:11
msgid ""
"Other names for this file are also supported for compatibility with other "
"agents, but note that the first file which matches in this list will be used:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:13
msgid "`.rules`"
msgstr "`.rules`"

#: src/ai/rules.md:14
msgid "`.cursorrules`"
msgstr "`.cursorrules`"

#: src/ai/rules.md:15
msgid "`.windsurfrules`"
msgstr "`.windsurfrules`"

#: src/ai/rules.md:16
msgid "`.clinerules`"
msgstr "`.clinerules`"

#: src/ai/rules.md:17
msgid "`.github/copilot-instructions.md`"
msgstr "`.github/copilot-instructions.md`"

#: src/ai/rules.md:18
msgid "`AGENT.md`"
msgstr "`AGENT.md`"

#: src/ai/rules.md:19
msgid "`AGENTS.md`"
msgstr "`AGENTS.md`"

#: src/ai/rules.md:20
msgid "`CLAUDE.md`"
msgstr "`CLAUDE.md`"

#: src/ai/rules.md:21
msgid "`GEMINI.md`"
msgstr "`GEMINI.md`"

#: src/ai/rules.md:23
msgid "Rules Library"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:25
msgid ""
"The Rules Library is an interface for writing and managing rules. It's a "
"full editor with syntax highlighting and all standard keybindings."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:28
msgid ""
"You can also use the inline assistant right in the rules editor, allowing "
"you to get quick LLM support for writing rules."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:30
msgid "Opening the Rules Library"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:32
msgid "Open the Agent Panel."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:33
msgid "Click on the Agent menu (`...`) in the top right corner."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:34
msgid "Select `Rules...` from the dropdown."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:36
msgid ""
"You can also open it by running the <code class=\"hljs\">agent: open rules "
"library</code> action or through the <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-alt-l\\|"
"ctrl-alt-l</kbd> keybinding."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:38
msgid "Managing Rules"
msgstr "管理規則"

#: src/ai/rules.md:40
msgid ""
"Once a rules file is selected, you can edit it directly in the built-in "
"editor. Its title can be changed from the editor title bar as well."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:43
msgid ""
"Rules can be duplicated, deleted, or added to the default rules using the "
"buttons in the rules editor."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:45
msgid "Creating Rules"
msgstr "建立規則"

#: src/ai/rules.md:47
msgid ""
"To create a rule file, simply open the `Rules Library` and click the `+` "
"button. Rules files are stored locally and can be accessed from the library "
"at any time."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:50
msgid "For guidance on writing effective rules:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:52
msgid ""
"[Anthropic: Prompt Engineering](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/build-"
"with-claude/prompt-engineering/overview)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:53
msgid ""
"[OpenAI: Prompt Engineering](https://platform.openai.com/docs/guides/prompt-"
"engineering)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:57
msgid ""
"You can @-mention every rule created through the Rules Library. This allows "
"you to quickly reach for reusable prompts, saving the time to type them out "
"every time you need to use them."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:60
msgid "Default Rules"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:62
msgid ""
"All rules in the Rules Library can be set as a default rule, which means "
"they’re automatically inserted into context for every new Agent Panel "
"interaction."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:64
msgid ""
"You can set any rule as the default by clicking the paper clip icon button "
"in the top-right of the rule editor in the Rules Library."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:66
msgid "Migrating from Prompt Library"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:68
msgid ""
"Previously, the Rules Library was called the \"Prompt Library\". The new "
"rules system replaces the Prompt Library except in a few specific cases, "
"which are outlined below."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/rules.md:71
msgid "Slash Commands in Rules"
msgstr "規則中的斜線命令"

#: src/ai/rules.md:73
msgid ""
"Previously, it was possible to use slash commands (now @-mentions) in custom "
"prompts (now rules). There is currently no support for using @-mentions in "
"rules files."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/subscription.md:3
msgid "Subscription"
msgstr "訂閱方案"

#: src/ai/subscription.md:5
msgid ""
"Zed's hosted models are offered via subscription to Zed Pro or Zed Business."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/subscription.md:7
msgid ""
"You can use [your own API keys](./llm-providers.md) or [external agents](./"
"external-agents.md) without a Zed subscription."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/subscription.md:9
msgid ""
"See the following pages for specific aspects of our subscription offering:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/subscription.md:11
msgid ""
"[Models](./models.md): Overview of the models offered by Zed's subscriptions."
msgstr "[模型](./models.md)：Zed 訂閱方案所提供的模型概覽。"

#: src/ai/subscription.md:13
msgid ""
"[Plans and Usage](./plans-and-usage.md): Outlines Zed's plans and how usage "
"is measured."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/subscription.md:15
msgid ""
"[Billing](./billing.md): Billing policies and procedures, and how to update "
"or view various billing settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:3
msgid "Billing"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:5
msgid ""
"This page covers billing for Zed's [subscription plans](./subscription.md). "
"For details on what's included in each plan and how token usage works, see "
"[Plans and Usage](./plans-and-usage.md)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:7
msgid ""
"We use Stripe as our payments provider, and Orb for invoicing and metering. "
"All Pro plans require payment via credit card or other supported payment "
"method. For invoice-based billing, a Business plan is required. Contact "
"[sales@zed.dev](mailto:sales@zed.dev) for more information."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:10
msgid "Billing Information"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:12
msgid ""
"Access billing information and settings at [dashboard.zed.dev/account]"
"(https://dashboard.zed.dev/account). This page embeds data from Orb, our "
"invoicing and metering partner."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:15
msgid "Billing Cycles"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:17
msgid ""
"Zed is billed on a monthly basis based on the date you initially subscribe. "
"You'll receive _at least_ one invoice from Zed each month you're subscribed "
"to Zed Pro, and more than one if you use more than $10 in incremental token "
"spend within the month."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:19
msgid "Threshold Billing"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:21
msgid ""
"Zed utilizes threshold billing to ensure timely collection of owed monies "
"and prevent abuse. Every time your usage of Zed's hosted models crosses a "
"$10 spend threshold, a new invoice is generated, and the threshold resets to "
"$0."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:23
msgid "For example,"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:25
msgid "You subscribe on February 1. Your first invoice is $10."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:26
msgid ""
"You use $12 of incremental tokens in the month of February, with the first "
"$10 spent on February 15. You'll receive an invoice for $10 on February 15"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:27
msgid ""
"On March 1, you receive an invoice for $12: $10 (March Pro subscription) and "
"$2 in leftover token spend, since your usage didn't cross the $10 threshold."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:29
msgid "Payment Failures"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:31
msgid ""
"If payment of an invoice fails, Zed will block usage of our hosted models "
"until the payment is complete. Email [billing-support@zed.dev](mailto:"
"billing-support@zed.dev) for assistance."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:33
msgid "Invoice History"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:35
msgid ""
"You can access your invoice history by navigating to [dashboard.zed.dev/"
"account](https://dashboard.zed.dev/account) and clicking `Invoice history` "
"within the embedded Orb portal."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:37
msgid ""
"If you require historical Stripe invoices, email [billing-support@zed.dev]"
"(mailto:billing-support@zed.dev)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:39
msgid "Updating Billing Information"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:41
msgid ""
"Email [billing-support@zed.dev](mailto:billing-support@zed.dev) for help "
"updating payment methods, names, addresses, and tax information."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:43
msgid "Self-service billing updates will be available in a future release."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:45
msgid ""
"Please note that changes to billing information will **only** affect future "
"invoices — **we cannot modify historical invoices**."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:47
msgid "Sales Tax"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:49
msgid ""
"Zed partners with [Sphere](https://www.getsphere.com/) to calculate indirect "
"tax rate for invoices, based on customer location and the product being "
"sold. Tax is listed as a separate line item on invoices, based "
"preferentially on your billing address, followed by the card issue country "
"known to Stripe."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:51
msgid ""
"If you have a VAT/GST ID, you can add it at during checkout. Check the box "
"that denotes you as a business."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/billing.md:53
msgid ""
"Please note that changes to VAT/GST IDs and address will **only** affect "
"future invoices — **we cannot modify historical invoices**. Questions or "
"issues can be directed to [billing-support@zed.dev](mailto:billing-"
"support@zed.dev)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/models.md:3
msgid "Models"
msgstr ""

