#: src/migrate/intellij.md:133
msgid "No Indexing"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:135
msgid ""
"If you've used IntelliJ on large projects, you know the wait: \"Indexing..."
"\" can take anywhere from 30 seconds to 15 minutes depending on project "
"size. IntelliJ builds a comprehensive index of your entire codebase to power "
"its code intelligence, and it re-indexes when dependencies change or after "
"builds."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:137
msgid ""
"Zed doesn't index. You open a folder and start working immediately. File "
"search and navigation work instantly regardless of project size."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:139
msgid ""
"IntelliJ's index powers features like finding all usages across your entire "
"codebase, understanding class hierarchies, and detecting dead code. Zed "
"delegates this work to language servers, which may not analyze at the same "
"depth."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:141 src/migrate/intellij.md:161
#: src/migrate/intellij.md:179 src/migrate/intellij.md:213
msgid "**How to adapt:**"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:143
msgid ""
"For project-wide symbol search, use `Cmd+O` / Go to Symbol (relies on your "
"language server)"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:144
msgid "For finding files by name, use `Cmd+Shift+O` / Go to File"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:145
msgid ""
"For text search across files, use `Cmd+Shift+F`—this is fast even on large "
"codebases"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:146
msgid ""
"If you need deep static analysis for JVM code, consider running IntelliJ's "
"inspections as a separate step or using standalone tools like Checkstyle, "
"PMD, or SpotBugs"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:148
msgid "LSP vs. Native Language Intelligence"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:150
msgid ""
"IntelliJ has its own language analysis engine built from scratch for each "
"supported language. For Java, Kotlin, and other JVM languages, this engine "
"understands your code thoroughly: it resolves types, tracks data flow, knows "
"about framework annotations, and offers dozens of specialized refactorings."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:152
msgid ""
"Zed uses the Language Server Protocol (LSP) for code intelligence. Each "
"language has its own server: `jdtls` for Java, `rust-analyzer` for Rust, and "
"so on."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:154
msgid ""
"For some languages, the LSP experience is excellent. TypeScript, Rust, and "
"Go have mature language servers that provide fast, accurate completions, "
"diagnostics, and refactorings. For JVM languages, the gap might be more "
"noticeable. The Eclipse-based Java language server is capable, but it won't "
"match IntelliJ's depth for things like:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:156
msgid "Spring and Jakarta EE annotation processing"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:157
msgid ""
"Complex refactorings (extract interface, pull members up, change signature "
"with all callers)"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:158
msgid "Framework-aware inspections"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:159
msgid "Automatic import optimization with custom ordering rules"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:163
msgid ""
"Use `Alt+Enter` for available code actions—the list will vary by language "
"server"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:164
msgid ""
"For Java, ensure `jdtls` is properly configured with your JDK path in "
"settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:166
msgid "No Project Model"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:168
msgid ""
"IntelliJ manages projects through `.idea` folders containing XML "
"configuration files, `.iml` module definitions, SDK assignments, and run "
"configurations. This model enables IntelliJ to understand multi-module "
"projects, manage dependencies automatically, and persist complex run/debug "
"setups."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:170
msgid ""
"Zed has no project model. A project is a folder. There's no wizard, no SDK "
"selection screen, no module configuration."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:172
msgid "This means:"
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:174
msgid "Build commands are manual. Zed doesn't detect Maven or Gradle projects."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:175
msgid "Run configurations don't exist. You define tasks or use the terminal."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:176
msgid ""
"SDK management is external. Your language server uses whatever JDK is on "
"your PATH."
msgstr ""

#: src/migrate/intellij.md:177
msgid ""
"There are no module boundaries. Zed sees folders, not project structure."
msgstr ""

