#: src/configuring-zed.md:597
msgid "Direnv Integration"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-zed.md:599
msgid ""
"Description: Settings for [direnv](https://direnv.net/) integration. "
"Requires `direnv` to be installed. `direnv` integration make it possible to "
"use the environment variables set by a `direnv` configuration to detect some "
"language servers in `$PATH` instead of installing them. It also allows for "
"those environment variables to be used in tasks."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-zed.md:602
msgid "Setting: `load_direnv`"
msgstr "設定：`load_direnv`"

#: src/configuring-zed.md:603
msgid "Default: `\"direct\"`"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-zed.md:607
msgid "There are three options to choose from:"
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-zed.md:609
msgid ""
"`shell_hook`: Use the shell hook to load direnv. This relies on direnv to "
"activate upon entering the directory. Supports POSIX shells and fish."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-zed.md:610
msgid ""
"`direct`: Use `direnv export json` to load direnv. This will load direnv "
"directly without relying on the shell hook and might cause some "
"inconsistencies. This allows direnv to work with any shell."
msgstr ""

#: src/configuring-zed.md:611
msgid ""
"`disabled`: No shell environment will be loaded automatically; direnv must "
"be invoked manually (e.g. with `direnv exec`) to be used."
msgstr ""

