#: src/extensions/languages.md:210
msgid "The `indents.scm` file defines indentation rules."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:212
msgid "Here's an example from an `indents.scm` file for JSON:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:214
msgid ""
"```scheme\n"
"(array \"]\" @end) @indent\n"
"(object \"}\" @end) @indent\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:219
msgid ""
"This query marks the end of arrays and objects for indentation purposes."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:223
msgid "@end"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:223
msgid "Captures closing brackets and braces"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:224
msgid "@indent"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:224
msgid "Captures entire arrays and objects for indentation"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:228
msgid ""
"The `injections.scm` file defines rules for embedding one language within "
"another, such as code blocks in Markdown or SQL queries in Python strings."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:230
msgid "Here's an example from an `injections.scm` file for Markdown:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:232
msgid ""
"```scheme\n"
"(fenced_code_block\n"
"  (info_string\n"
"    (language) @injection.language)\n"
"  (code_fence_content) @injection.content)\n"
"\n"
"((inline) @content\n"
" (#set! injection.language \"markdown-inline\"))\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:242
msgid ""
"This query identifies fenced code blocks, capturing the language specified "
"in the info string and the content within the block. It also captures inline "
"content and sets its language to \"markdown-inline\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:246
msgid "@injection.language"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:246
msgid "Captures the language identifier for a code block"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:247
msgid "@injection.content"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:247
msgid "Captures the content to be treated as a different language"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:249
msgid ""
"Note that we couldn't use JSON as an example here because it doesn't support "
"language injections."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:253
msgid ""
"The `overrides.scm` file defines syntactic _scopes_ that can be used to "
"override certain editor settings within specific language constructs."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:255
msgid ""
"For example, there is a language-specific setting called `word_characters` "
"that controls which non-alphabetic characters are considered part of a word, "
"for example when you double click to select a variable. In JavaScript, \"$\" "
"and \"#\" are considered word characters."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:257
msgid ""
"There is also a language-specific setting called "
"`completion_query_characters` that controls which characters trigger "
"autocomplete suggestions. In JavaScript, when your cursor is within a "
"_string_, `-` should be considered a completion query character. To achieve "
"this, the JavaScript `overrides.scm` file contains the following pattern:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:266
msgid "And the JavaScript `config.toml` contains this setting:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:268
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"word_characters = [\"#\", \"$\"]\n"
"\n"
"[overrides.string]\n"
"completion_query_characters = [\"-\"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:275
msgid ""
"You can also disable certain auto-closing brackets in a specific scope. For "
"example, to prevent auto-closing `'` within strings, you could put the "
"following in the JavaScript `config.toml`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:277
msgid ""
"```toml\n"
"brackets = [\n"
"  { start = \"'\", end = \"'\", close = true, newline = false, not_in = "
"[\"string\"] },\n"
"  # other pairs...\n"
"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:284
msgid "Range inclusivity"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:286
msgid ""
"By default, the ranges defined in `overrides.scm` are _exclusive_. So in the "
"case above, if your cursor was _outside_ the quotation marks delimiting the "
"string, the `string` scope would not take effect. Sometimes, you may want to "
"make the range _inclusive_. You can do this by adding the `.inclusive` "
"suffix to the capture name in the query."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:288
msgid ""
"For example, in JavaScript, we also disable auto-closing of single quotes "
"within comments. And the comment scope must extend all the way to the "
"newline after a line comment. To achieve this, the JavaScript `overrides."
"scm` contains the following pattern:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:294
msgid "Text objects"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:296
msgid ""
"The `textobjects.scm` file defines rules for navigating by text objects. "
"This was added in Zed v0.165 and is currently used only in Vim mode."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:298
msgid ""
"Vim provides two levels of granularity for navigating around files. Section-"
"by-section with `[]` etc., and method-by-method with `]m` etc. Even "
"languages that don't support functions and classes can work well by defining "
"similar concepts. For example CSS defines a rule-set as a method, and a "
"media-query as a class."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:300
msgid ""
"For languages with closures, these typically should not count as functions "
"in Zed. This is best-effort, however, because languages like JavaScript do "
"not syntactically differentiate between closures and top-level function "
"declarations."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:302
msgid ""
"For languages with declarations like C, provide queries that match `@class."
"around` or `@function.around`. The `if` and `ic` text objects will default "
"to these if there is no inside."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:304
msgid ""
"If you are not sure what to put in textobjects.scm, both [nvim-treesitter-"
"textobjects](https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-"
"textobjects), and the [Helix editor](https://github.com/helix-editor/helix) "
"have queries for many languages. You can refer to the Zed [built-in "
"languages](https://github.com/zed-industries/zed/tree/main/crates/languages/"
"src) to see how to adapt these."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:306
msgid "Vim mode"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:308
msgid "@function.around"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:308
msgid "An entire function definition or equivalent small section of a file."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:308
msgid "`[m`, `]m`, `[M`,`]M` motions. `af` text object"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:309
msgid "@function.inside"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:309
msgid "The function body (the stuff within the braces)."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:309
msgid "`if` text object"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:310
msgid "@class.around"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:310
msgid "An entire class definition or equivalent large section of a file."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:310
msgid "`[[`, `]]`, `[]`, `][` motions. `ac` text object"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:311
msgid "@class.inside"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:311
msgid "The contents of a class definition."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:311
msgid "`ic` text object"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:312
msgid "@comment.around"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:312
msgid "An entire comment (e.g. all adjacent line comments, or a block comment)"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:312
msgid "`gc` text object"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:313
msgid "@comment.inside"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:313
msgid "The contents of a comment"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:313
msgid "`igc` text object (rarely supported)"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:317
msgid ""
"```scheme\n"
"; include only the content of the method in the function\n"
"(method_definition\n"
"    body: (_\n"
"        \"{\"\n"
"        (_)* @function.inside\n"
"        \"}\")) @function.around\n"
"\n"
"; match function.around for declarations with no body\n"
"(function_signature_item) @function.around\n"
"\n"
"; join all adjacent comments into one\n"
"(comment)+ @comment.around\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:334
msgid ""
"The `redactions.scm` file defines text redaction rules. When collaborating "
"and sharing your screen, it makes sure that certain syntax nodes are "
"rendered in a redacted mode to avoid them from leaking."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:336
msgid "Here's an example from a `redactions.scm` file for JSON:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:345
msgid ""
"This query marks number and string values in key-value pairs and arrays for "
"redaction."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:349
msgid "@redact"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:349
msgid "Captures values to be redacted"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:353
msgid "The `runnables.scm` file defines rules for detecting runnable code."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:355
msgid "Here's an example from a `runnables.scm` file for JSON:"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:357
msgid ""
"```scheme\n"
"(\n"
"    (document\n"
"        (object\n"
"            (pair\n"
"                key: (string\n"
"                    (string_content) @_name\n"
"                    (#eq? @_name \"scripts\")\n"
"                )\n"
"                value: (object\n"
"                    (pair\n"
"                        key: (string (string_content) @run @script)\n"
"                    )\n"
"                )\n"
"            )\n"
"        )\n"
"    )\n"
"    (#set! tag package-script)\n"
"    (#set! tag composer-script)\n"
")\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:379
msgid ""
"This query detects runnable scripts in package.json and composer.json files."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:381
msgid ""
"The `@run` capture specifies where the run button should appear in the "
"editor. Other captures, except those prefixed with an underscore, are "
"exposed as environment variables with a prefix of "
"`ZED_CUSTOM_$(capture_name)` when running the code."
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:385
msgid "@\\_name"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:385
msgid "Captures the \"scripts\" key"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:386
msgid "@run"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:386
msgid "Captures the script name"
msgstr ""

#: src/extensions/languages.md:387
