#: src/languages/java.md:26
msgid "Quick start and configuration"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/java.md:28
msgid "For the majority of users, Java support should work out of the box."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/java.md:30
msgid ""
"It is generally recommended to open projects with the Zed-project root at "
"the Java project root folder (where you would commonly have your `pom.xml` "
"or `build.gradle` file)."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/java.md:32
msgid ""
"By default the extension will download and run the latest official version "
"of JDTLS for you, but this requires Java version 21 to be available on your "
"system via either the `$JAVA_HOME` environment variable or as a `java(.exe)` "
"executable on your `$PATH`. If your project requires a lower Java version in "
"the environment, you can specify a different JDK to use for running JDTLS "
"via the `java_home` configuration option."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/java.md:34
msgid ""
"You can provide a **custom launch script for JDTLS**, by adding an "
"executable named `jdtls` (or `jdtls.bat` on Windows) to your `$PATH` "
"environment variable. If this is present, the extension will skip "
"downloading and launching a managed instance and use the one from the "
"environment."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/java.md:36
msgid ""
"To support [Lombok](https://projectlombok.org/), the lombok-jar must be "
"downloaded and registered as a Java-Agent when launching JDTLS. By default "
"the extension automatically takes care of that, but in case you don't want "
"that you can set the `lombok_support` configuration-option to `false`."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/java.md:38
msgid ""
"Here is a common `settings.json` including the above mentioned "
"configurations:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/java.md:40
msgid ""
"```jsonc\n"
"{\n"
"  \"lsp\": {\n"
"    \"jdtls\": {\n"
"      \"settings\": {\n"
"        \"java_home\": \"/path/to/your/JDK21+\",\n"
"        \"lombok_support\": true,\n"
"      },\n"
"    },\n"
"  },\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```jsonc\n"
"{\n"
"  \"lsp\": {\n"
"    \"jdtls\": {\n"
"      \"settings\": {\n"
"        \"java_home\": \"/path/to/your/JDK21+\",\n"
"        \"lombok_support\": true,\n"
"      },\n"
"    },\n"
"  },\n"
"}\n"
"```"

#: src/languages/java.md:55
msgid ""
"Debug support is enabled via our [Fork of Java Debug](https://github.com/zed-"
"industries/java-debug), which the extension will automatically download and "
"start for you. Please refer to the [Debugger Documentation](https://zed.dev/"
"docs/debugger#getting-started) for general information about how debugging "
"works in Zed."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/java.md:57
msgid ""
"To get started with Java, click the `edit debug.json` button in the Debug "
"menu, and replace the contents of the file with the following:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/java.md:59
msgid ""
"```jsonc\n"
"[\n"
"  {\n"
"    \"adapter\": \"Java\",\n"
"    \"request\": \"launch\",\n"
"    \"label\": \"Launch Debugger\",\n"
"    // if your project has multiple entry points, specify the one to use:\n"
"    // \"mainClass\": \"com.myorganization.myproject.MyMainClass\",\n"
"    //\n"
"    // this effectively sets a breakpoint at your program entry:\n"
"    \"stopOnEntry\": true,\n"
"    // the working directory for the debug process\n"
"    \"cwd\": \"$ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT\",\n"
"  },\n"
"]\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/java.md:76
msgid ""
"You should then be able to start a new Debug Session with the \"Launch "
"Debugger\" scenario from the debug menu."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/java.md:78
msgid "Launch Scripts (aka Tasks) in Windows"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/java.md:80
msgid ""
"This extension provides tasks for running your application and tests from "
"within Zed via little play buttons next to tests/entry points. However, due "
"to current limitations of Zed's extension interface, we can not provide "
"scripts that will work across Maven and Gradle on both Windows and Unix-"
"compatible systems, so out of the box the launch scripts only work on Mac "
"and Linux."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/java.md:82
msgid ""
"There is a fairly straightforward fix that you can apply to make it work on "
"Windows by supplying your own task scripts. Please see [this Issue](https://"
"github.com/zed-extensions/java/issues/94) for information on how to do that "
"and read the [Tasks section in Zeds documentation](https://zed.dev/docs/"
"tasks) for more information."
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/java.md:84
msgid "Advanced Configuration/JDTLS initialization Options"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/java.md:86
msgid ""
"JDTLS provides many configuration options that can be passed via the "
"`initialize` LSP-request. The extension will pass the JSON-object from `lsp."
"jdtls.settings.initialization_options` in your settings on to JDTLS. Please "
"refer to the [JDTLS Configuration Wiki Page](https://github.com/eclipse-"
"jdtls/eclipse.jdt.ls/wiki/Running-the-JAVA-LS-server-from-the-command-"
"line#initialize-request) for the available options and values. Below is an "
"example `settings.json` that would pass on the example configuration from "
"the above wiki page to JDTLS:"
msgstr ""

#: src/languages/java.md:88
msgid ""
"```jsonc\n"
"{\n"
"  \"lsp\": {\n"
"    \"jdtls\": {\n"
"      \"settings\": {\n"
"        // this will be sent to JDTLS as initializationOptions:\n"
"        \"initialization_options\": {\n"
"          \"bundles\": [],\n"
"          // use this if your zed project root folder is not the same as the "
"java project root:\n"
"          \"workspaceFolders\": [\"file:///home/snjeza/Project\"],\n"
"          \"settings\": {\n"
"            \"java\": {\n"
"              \"home\": \"/usr/local/jdk-9.0.1\",\n"
"              \"errors\": {\n"
"                \"incompleteClasspath\": {\n"
"                  \"severity\": \"warning\",\n"
"                },\n"
"              },\n"
"              \"configuration\": {\n"
"                \"updateBuildConfiguration\": \"interactive\",\n"
"                \"maven\": {\n"
"                  \"userSettings\": null,\n"
"                },\n"
"              },\n"
"              \"import\": {\n"
"                \"gradle\": {\n"
"                  \"enabled\": true,\n"
"                },\n"
"                \"maven\": {\n"
"                  \"enabled\": true,\n"
"                },\n"
"                \"exclusions\": [\n"
"                  \"**/node_modules/**\",\n"
"                  \"**/.metadata/**\",\n"
"                  \"**/archetype-resources/**\",\n"
"                  \"**/META-INF/maven/**\",\n"
"                  \"/**/test/**\",\n"
"                ],\n"
"              },\n"
"              \"referencesCodeLens\": {\n"
"                \"enabled\": false,\n"
"              },\n"
"              \"signatureHelp\": {\n"
"                \"enabled\": false,\n"
"              },\n"
"              \"implementationCodeLens\": \"all\",\n"
"              \"format\": {\n"
"                \"enabled\": true,\n"
"              },\n"
"              \"saveActions\": {\n"
"                \"organizeImports\": false,\n"
"              },\n"
"              \"contentProvider\": {\n"
"                \"preferred\": null,\n"
"              },\n"
"              \"autobuild\": {\n"
"                \"enabled\": false,\n"
"              },\n"
"              \"completion\": {\n"
"                \"favoriteStaticMembers\": [\n"
"                  \"org.junit.Assert.*\",\n"
"                  \"org.junit.Assume.*\",\n"
"                  \"org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*\",\n"
"                  \"org.junit.jupiter.api.Assumptions.*\",\n"
"                  \"org.junit.jupiter.api.DynamicContainer.*\",\n"
"                  \"org.junit.jupiter.api.DynamicTest.*\",\n"
"                ],\n"
"                \"importOrder\": [\"java\", \"javax\", \"com\", \"org\"],\n"
"              },\n"
"            },\n"
"          },\n"
"        },\n"
"      },\n"
"    },\n"
"  },\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

