msgid ""
"If this command returns no output, Zed is using RandR (X11's monitor "
"management extension) to automatically calculate the scale factor based on "
"your monitor's reported resolution and physical dimensions."
msgstr ""

#: src/linux.md:330
msgid "Option 1: Set Xft.dpi (X Resources Database)"
msgstr ""

#: src/linux.md:332
msgid ""
"`Xft.dpi` is a standard X11 setting that many applications use for "
"consistent font and UI scaling. Setting this ensures Zed scales the same way "
"as other X11 applications that respect this setting."
msgstr ""

#: src/linux.md:334
msgid "Edit or create the `~/.Xresources` file:"
msgstr ""

#: src/linux.md:340
msgid "Add this line with your desired DPI:"
msgstr ""

#: src/linux.md:346
msgid "Common DPI values:"
msgstr ""

#: src/linux.md:348
msgid "`96` for standard 1x scaling"
msgstr ""

#: src/linux.md:349
msgid "`144` for 1.5x scaling"
msgstr ""

#: src/linux.md:350
msgid "`192` for 2x scaling"
msgstr ""

#: src/linux.md:351
msgid "`288` for 3x scaling"
msgstr ""

#: src/linux.md:353
msgid "Load the configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: src/linux.md:359
msgid "Restart Zed for the changes to take effect."
msgstr ""

#: src/linux.md:361
msgid "Option 2: Use the GPUI_X11_SCALE_FACTOR environment variable"
msgstr ""

#: src/linux.md:363
msgid ""
"This Zed-specific environment variable directly sets the scale factor, "
"bypassing all automatic detection."
msgstr ""

#: src/linux.md:366
msgid "1.5"
msgstr ""

#: src/linux.md:369
msgid ""
"You can use decimal values (e.g., `1.25`, `1.5`, `2.0`) or set "
"`GPUI_X11_SCALE_FACTOR=randr` to force RandR-based detection even when `Xft."
