#: src/debugger.md:145
msgid "Breakpoints"
msgstr ""

#: src/debugger.md:147
msgid ""
"To set a breakpoint, simply click next to the line number in the editor "
"gutter. Breakpoints can be tweaked depending on your needs; to access "
"additional options of a given breakpoint, right-click on the breakpoint icon "
"in the gutter and select the desired option. At present, you can:"
msgstr ""

#: src/debugger.md:151
msgid ""
"Add a log to a breakpoint, which will output a log message whenever that "
"breakpoint is hit."
msgstr ""

#: src/debugger.md:152
msgid ""
"Make the breakpoint conditional, which will only stop at the breakpoint when "
"the condition is met. The syntax for conditions is adapter-specific."
msgstr ""

#: src/debugger.md:153
msgid ""
"Add a hit count to a breakpoint, which will only stop at the breakpoint "
"after it's hit a certain number of times."
msgstr ""

#: src/debugger.md:154
msgid ""
"Disable a breakpoint, which will prevent it from being hit while leaving it "
"visible in the gutter."
msgstr ""

#: src/debugger.md:156
msgid ""
"Some debug adapters (e.g. CodeLLDB and JavaScript) will also _verify_ "
"whether your breakpoints can be hit; breakpoints that cannot be hit are "
"surfaced more prominently in the UI."
