#: src/tasks.md:3
msgid ""
"Zed supports ways to spawn (and rerun) commands using its integrated "
"terminal to output the results. These commands can read a limited subset of "
"Zed state (such as a path to the file currently being edited or selected "
"text)."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:8
msgid "\"Example task\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:9
msgid "\"for i in {1..5}; do echo \\\"Hello $i/5\\\"; sleep 1; done\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:10
msgid ""
"//\"args\": [],\n"
"    // Env overrides for the command, will be appended to the terminal's "
"environment from the settings.\n"
"    \"env\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:12
msgid "\"foo\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:13
msgid ""
"// Current working directory to spawn the command into, defaults to current "
"project root.\n"
"    //\"cwd\": \"/path/to/working/directory\",\n"
"    // Whether to use a new terminal tab or reuse the existing one to spawn "
"the process, defaults to `false`.\n"
"    \"use_new_terminal\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:17
msgid ""
"// Whether to allow multiple instances of the same task to be run, or rather "
"wait for the existing ones to finish, defaults to `false`.\n"
"    \"allow_concurrent_runs\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:19
msgid ""
"// What to do with the terminal pane and tab, after the command was "
"started:\n"
"    // * `always` — always show the task's pane, and focus the corresponding "
"tab in it (default)\n"
"    // * `no_focus` — always show the task's pane, add the task's tab in it, "
"but don't focus it\n"
"    // * `never` — do not alter focus, but still add/reuse the task's tab in "
"its pane\n"
"    \"reveal\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:24
msgid ""
"// What to do with the terminal pane and tab, after the command has "
"finished:\n"
"    // * `never` — Do nothing when the command finishes (default)\n"
"    // * `always` — always hide the terminal tab, hide the pane also if it "
"was the last tab in it\n"
"    // * `on_success` — hide the terminal tab on task success only, "
"otherwise behaves similar to `always`\n"
"    \"hide\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:29
msgid ""
"// Which shell to use when running a task inside the terminal.\n"
"    // May take 3 values:\n"
"    // 1. (default) Use the system's default terminal configuration in /etc/"
"passwd\n"
"    //      \"shell\": \"system\"\n"
"    // 2. A program:\n"
"    //      \"shell\": {\n"
"    //        \"program\": \"sh\"\n"
"    //      }\n"
"    // 3. A program with arguments:\n"
"    //     \"shell\": {\n"
"    //         \"with_arguments\": {\n"
"    //           \"program\": \"/bin/bash\",\n"
"    //           \"args\": [\"--login\"]\n"
"    //         }\n"
"    //     }\n"
"    \"shell\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:45
msgid ""
"// Whether to show the task line in the output of the spawned task, defaults "
"to `true`.\n"
"    \"show_summary\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:47
msgid ""
"// Whether to show the command line in the output of the spawned task, "
"defaults to `true`.\n"
"    \"show_command\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:49
msgid ""
"// Represents the tags for inline runnable indicators, or spawning multiple "
"tasks at once.\n"
"    // \"tags\": []\n"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:55
msgid ""
"There are two actions that drive the workflow of using tasks: `task: spawn` "
"and `task: rerun`. `task: spawn` opens a modal with all available tasks in "
"the current file. `task: rerun` reruns the most recently spawned task. You "
"can also rerun tasks from the task modal."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:59
msgid ""
"By default, rerunning tasks reuses the same terminal (due to the "
"`\"use_new_terminal\": false` default) but waits for the previous task to "
"finish before starting (due to the `\"allow_concurrent_runs\": false` "
"default)."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:61
msgid ""
"Keep `\"use_new_terminal\": false` and set `\"allow_concurrent_runs\": true` "
"to allow cancelling previous tasks on rerun."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:63
msgid "Task templates"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:65
msgid "Tasks can be defined:"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:67
msgid ""
"in the global `tasks.json` file; such tasks are available in all Zed "
"projects you work on. This file is usually located in `~/.config/zed/tasks."
"json`. You can edit them by using the `zed: open tasks` action."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:68
msgid ""
"in the worktree-specific (local) `.zed/tasks.json` file; such tasks are "
"available only when working on a project with that worktree included. You "
"can edit worktree-specific tasks by using the `zed: open project tasks` "
"action."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:69
msgid ""
"on the fly with [oneshot tasks](#oneshot-tasks). These tasks are project-"
"specific and do not persist across sessions."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:70
msgid "by language extension."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:72
msgid "Variables"
msgstr "變數"

#: src/tasks.md:74
msgid ""
"Zed tasks act just like your shell; that also means that you can reference "
"environmental variables via sh-esque `$VAR_NAME` syntax. A couple of "
"additional environmental variables are set for your convenience. These "
"variables allow you to pull information from the current editor and use it "
"in your tasks. The following variables are available:"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:77
msgid "`ZED_COLUMN`: current line column"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:78
msgid "`ZED_ROW`: current line row"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:79
msgid ""
"`ZED_FILE`: absolute path of the currently opened file (e.g. `/Users/my-user/"
"path/to/project/src/main.rs`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:80
msgid "`ZED_FILENAME`: filename of the currently opened file (e.g. `main.rs`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:81
msgid ""
"`ZED_DIRNAME`: absolute path of the currently opened file with file name "
"stripped (e.g. `/Users/my-user/path/to/project/src`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:82
msgid ""
"`ZED_RELATIVE_FILE`: path of the currently opened file, relative to "
"`ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT` (e.g. `src/main.rs`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:83
msgid ""
"`ZED_RELATIVE_DIR`: path of the currently opened file's directory, relative "
"to `ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT` (e.g. `src`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:84
msgid ""
"`ZED_STEM`: stem (filename without extension) of the currently opened file "
"(e.g. `main`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:85
msgid ""
"`ZED_SYMBOL`: currently selected symbol; should match the last symbol shown "
"in a symbol breadcrumb (e.g. `mod tests > fn test_task_contexts`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:86
msgid "`ZED_SELECTED_TEXT`: currently selected text"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:87
msgid ""
"`ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT`: absolute path to the root of the current worktree. (e."
"g. `/Users/my-user/path/to/project`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:88
msgid ""
"`ZED_CUSTOM_RUST_PACKAGE`: (Rust-specific) name of the parent package of "
"$ZED_FILE source file."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:90
msgid "To use a variable in a task, prefix it with a dollar sign (`$`):"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:94 src/tasks.md:192 src/tasks.md:233
msgid "\"echo current file's path\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:95 src/tasks.md:234
msgid "\"echo $ZED_FILE\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:99
msgid ""
"You can also use verbose syntax that allows specifying a default if a given "
"variable is not available: `${ZED_FILE:default_value}`"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:101
msgid ""
"These environmental variables can also be used in tasks' `cwd`, `args`, and "
"`label` fields."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:103
msgid "Variable Quoting"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:105
msgid ""
"When working with paths containing spaces or other special characters, "
"please ensure variables are properly escaped."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:107
msgid "For example, instead of this (which will fail if the path has a space):"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:111 src/tasks.md:120 src/tasks.md:130
msgid "\"stat current file\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:112
msgid "\"stat $ZED_FILE\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:116
msgid "Provide the following:"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:121
msgid "\"stat\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:126
msgid "Or explicitly include escaped quotes like so:"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:131
msgid "\"stat \\\"$ZED_FILE\\\"\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:135
msgid "Task filtering based on variables"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:137
msgid ""
"Task definitions with variables which are not present at the moment the task "
"list is determined are filtered out. For example, the following task will "
"appear in the spawn modal only if there is a text selection:"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:142
msgid "\"selected text\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:143
msgid "\"echo \\\"$ZED_SELECTED_TEXT\\\"\""
msgstr "\"echo \\\"$ZED_SELECTED_TEXT\\\"\""

#: src/tasks.md:147
msgid ""
"Set default values to such variables to have such tasks always displayed:"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:151
msgid "\"selected text with default\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:152
msgid "\"echo \\\"${ZED_SELECTED_TEXT:no text selected}\\\"\""
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:156
msgid "Oneshot tasks"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:158
msgid ""
"The same task modal opened via `task: spawn` supports arbitrary bash-like "
"command execution: type a command inside the modal text field, and use `opt-"
"enter` to spawn it."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:160
msgid ""
"The task modal persists these ad-hoc commands for the duration of the "
"session, `task: rerun` will also rerun such tasks if they were the last ones "
"spawned."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:162
msgid ""
"You can also adjust the currently selected task in a modal (`tab` is the "
"default key binding). Doing so will put its command into a prompt that can "
"then be edited & spawned as a oneshot task."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:164
msgid "Ephemeral tasks"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:166
msgid ""
"You can use the `cmd` modifier when spawning a task via a modal; tasks "
"spawned this way will not have their usage count increased (thus, they will "
"not be respawned with `task: rerun` and they won't have a high rank in the "
"task modal). The intended use of ephemeral tasks is to stay in the flow with "
"continuous `task: rerun` usage."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:169
msgid "More task rerun control"
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:171
msgid ""
"By default, tasks capture their variables into a context once, and this "
"\"resolved task\" is being rerun always."
msgstr ""

#: src/tasks.md:173
msgid ""
"This can be controlled with the `\"reevaluate_context\"` argument to the "
"task: setting it to `true` will force the task to be reevaluated before each "
"run."
msgstr ""

