#: src/command-palette.md:5
msgid ""
"The Command Palette is the main way to access actions in Zed. Its keybinding "
"is one of the first shortcuts to learn: <kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-shift-"
"p\\|ctrl-shift-p</kbd>."
msgstr ""

#: src/command-palette.md:9
msgid ""
"To try it, open the Command Palette and type `new file`. The command list "
"should narrow to `workspace: new file`. Press Return to create a new buffer."
msgstr ""

#: src/outline-panel.md:7
msgid ""
"When viewing a \"singleton\" buffer (i.e., a single file on a tab), the "
"outline panel works similarly to that of the outline modal－it displays the "
"outline of the current buffer's symbols. Each symbol entry shows its type "
"prefix (such as \"struct\", \"fn\", \"mod\", \"impl\") along with the symbol "
"name, helping you quickly identify what kind of symbol you're looking at. "
"Clicking on an entry allows you to jump to the associated section in the "
"file. The outline view will also automatically scroll to the section "
"associated with the current cursor position within the file."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:5
msgid ""
"The project panel shows a tree view of your workspace's files and "
"directories. Toggle it with <code class=\"hljs\">project panel: toggle "
"focus</code> (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-shift-e\\|ctrl-shift-e</kbd>), "
"or click the **Project Panel** button in the status bar."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:9
msgid "![Project Panel](https://images.zed.dev/docs/project-panel/panel.png)"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:11
msgid "Navigating"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:13
msgid ""
"Use the arrow keys to move through entries. <kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">right\\|right</kbd> expands a directory and <kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">left\\|left</kbd> collapses it. <kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-left\\|ctrl-left</kbd> collapses every directory at "
"once. Press <kbd class=\"keybinding\">space\\|space</kbd> or click to "
"preview a selected file, without giving it a permanent tab. Editing the file "
"or double-clicking it promotes it to a permanent tab."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:16
msgid "Auto-reveal"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:18
msgid ""
"By default, switching files in the editor will automatically highlight it in "
"the project panel and scroll it into view. This can be disabled with the "
"`project_panel.auto_reveal_entries` setting."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:22
msgid "Sticky Scroll"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:24
msgid ""
"When `project_panel.sticky_scroll` is enabled (the default), ancestor "
"directories pin themselves to the top of the panel as you scroll, so you "
"always know which directory you're on."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:27
msgid ""
"![Project Panel: Sticky Scroll Enabled](https://images.zed.dev/docs/project-"
"panel/sticky-scroll-true.png)"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:29
msgid ""
"![Project Panel: Sticky Scroll Disabled](https://images.zed.dev/docs/project-"
"panel/sticky-scroll-false.png)"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:31
msgid "Directory Folding"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:33
msgid ""
"When `project_panel.auto_fold_dirs` is enabled (the default), chains of "
"directories that each contain a single child directory are collapsed into "
"one row (for example, `src/utils/helpers` instead of three separate levels). "
"Right-click a folded directory and choose **Unfold Directory** to expand the "
"chain, or **Fold Directory** to collapse it again."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:39
msgid ""
"![Project Panel: Auto Fold Directories Enabled](https://images.zed.dev/docs/"
"project-panel/auto-fold-dirs-true.png)"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:41
msgid ""
"![Project Panel: Auto Fold Directories Disabled](https://images.zed.dev/docs/"
"project-panel/auto-fold-dirs-false.png)"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:43
msgid "Selecting Multiple Entries"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:45
msgid ""
"Hold `shift` while pressing the up/down arrow keys to mark additional "
"entries. Most file operations, like cut, copy, trash, delete and drag, apply "
"to the full set of marked entries."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:49
msgid ""
"When exactly two files are marked, <code class=\"hljs\">project panel: "
"compare marked files</code> (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">alt-d\\|alt-d</kbd>) "
"opens a diff view comparing them."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:52
msgid ""
"![Project Panel: Compare Marked Files](https://images.zed.dev/docs/project-"
"panel/compare-marked-files.png)"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:54
msgid "File Operations"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:56
msgid ""
"Right-click an entry to see the full list of available operations, or use "
"the keybindings below."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:59
msgid "Creating Files and Directories"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:61
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: new file</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-n\\|ctrl-n</kbd>) creates a new file inside the "
"selected directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:63
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: new directory</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">alt-cmd-n\\|alt-ctrl-n</kbd>) creates a new directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:66
msgid ""
"An inline editor appears so you can type the name. Press `enter` to confirm "
"or `escape` to cancel."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:69
msgid "Renaming"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:71
msgid ""
"Press <kbd class=\"keybinding\">f2\\|f2</kbd> to rename the selected entry. "
"The filename stem is pre-selected so you can type a new name without "
"accidentally changing the extension. Press `enter` to confirm or `escape` to "
"cancel."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:76
msgid "Cut, Copy, and Paste"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:78
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: cut</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-x\\|ctrl-x</kbd>) marks entries for moving."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:80
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: copy</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-c\\|ctrl-c</kbd>) marks entries for copying."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:82
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: paste</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-v\\|ctrl-v</kbd>) places them in the selected "
"directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:85
msgid ""
"When pasting would create a name conflict, Zed appends a \"copy\" suffix (e."
"g., `file copy.txt`, `file copy 2.txt`). If a single file is pasted with a "
"generated suffix, the rename editor opens automatically so you can adjust "
"the name."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:89
msgid "Duplicate"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:91
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: duplicate</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-d\\|</kbd>) copies and pastes the selected entries "
"in one step."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:94
msgid "Trash and Delete"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:96
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: trash</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-backspace\\|delete</kbd>) moves entries to the "
"system trash."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:98
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: delete</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-alt-backspace\\|ctrl-delete</kbd>) permanently "
"deletes entries."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:101
msgid ""
"Both actions show a confirmation prompt listing the affected files. If any "
"of the files have unsaved changes, the prompt warns you."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:104
msgid "Drag and Drop"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:106
msgid ""
"Drag entries within the panel to move them. Hold `alt` while dropping to "
"copy instead of move. You can also drag files from your operating system's "
"file manager into the project panel to copy them into the project. Drag and "
"drop can be disabled with the `project_panel.drag_and_drop` setting."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:111
msgid "Git Integration"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:113
msgid ""
"When `project_panel.git_status` is enabled (the default), file and directory "
"names are tinted to reflect their git status—modified, added, deleted, "
"untracked, or conflicting."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:116
msgid ""
"Setting `project_panel.git_status_indicator` to `true` (disabled by default) "
"adds a letter badge next to each name: **M** (modified), **A** (added), "
"**D** (deleted), **U** (untracked) or **!** (conflict)."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:120
msgid ""
"![Project Panel: Git Integration](https://images.zed.dev/docs/project-panel/"
"git-status.png)"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:122
msgid ""
"Use <code class=\"hljs\">project panel: select next git entry</code> and "
"{#action project_panel::SelectPrevGitEntry} to jump between tracked files "
"with uncommitted changes. The right-click menu also offers **Restore File** "
"to discard changes and **View File History** to browse a file's commit log."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:129
msgid ""
"The `project_panel.show_diagnostics` setting controls whether error and "
"warning indicators appear on file and folder icons. Set it to `\"all\"` to "
"see both errors and warnings, `\"errors\"` for errors only, or `\"off\"` to "
"hide them. Diagnostics propagate upward—if a file deep in a directory has an "
"error, its ancestor folders show an indicator too."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:135
msgid ""
"Enable `project_panel.diagnostic_badges` (disabled by default) to display "
"numeric error and warning counts next to each entry. Use <code "
"class=\"hljs\">project panel: select next diagnostic</code> and <code "
"class=\"hljs\">project panel: select prev diagnostic</code> to navigate "
"between files that have diagnostics."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:140
msgid ""
"See also [Diagnostics & Quick Fixes](./diagnostics.md) for editor and tab "
"diagnostic settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:142
msgid "Filtering and Sorting"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:144
msgid "Hiding Files"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:146
msgid ""
"`project_panel.hide_gitignore` hides files matched by `.gitignore`. Toggle "
"this with <code class=\"hljs\">project panel: toggle hide git ignore</code>."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:148
msgid ""
"`project_panel.hide_hidden` hides dotfiles and other hidden entries. Toggle "
"with <code class=\"hljs\">project panel: toggle hide hidden</code>."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:151
msgid "Sorting"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:153
msgid "The `project_panel.sort_mode` setting controls grouping:"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:155
msgid ""
"`\"directories_first\"` (default) — directories appear before files at each "
"level."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:157
msgid "`\"files_first\"` — files appear before directories."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:158
msgid "`\"mixed\"` — directories and files are sorted together."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:160
msgid "The `project_panel.sort_order` setting controls name comparison:"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:162
msgid ""
"`\"default\"` — case-insensitive natural sort (`file2` before `file10`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:163
msgid "`\"upper\"` — uppercase names grouped first, then lowercase."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:164
msgid "`\"lower\"` — lowercase names grouped first, then uppercase."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:165
msgid "`\"unicode\"` — raw Unicode codepoint order with no case folding."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:167
msgid "Other Actions"
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:169
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: reveal in file manager</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">alt-cmd-r\\|alt-ctrl-r</kbd>) reveals the selected "
"entry in Finder / File Explorer."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:171
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: new search in directory</code> (<kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">cmd-alt-shift-f\\|ctrl-alt-shift-f</kbd>) opens a "
"project search scoped to the selected directory."
msgstr ""

#: src/project-panel.md:173
msgid ""
"<code class=\"hljs\">project panel: remove from project</code> removes a "
"workspace root folder from the project."
msgstr ""

#: src/tab-switcher.md:13
msgid ""
"When the Tab Switcher is opened using <kbd class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-tab\\|"
"ctrl-tab</kbd>, instead of running the <code class=\"hljs\">tab switcher: "
"toggle</code> from the command palette, it'll stay active as long as the "
"<kbd class=\"keybinding\">ctrl</kbd> key is held down."
msgstr ""

#: src/tab-switcher.md:25
msgid ""
"The Tab Switcher can also be opened with either <code class=\"hljs\">tab "
"switcher: toggle</code> (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-tab\\|ctrl-tab</"
"kbd>) or <code class=\"hljs\">tab switcher: toggle all</code>."
msgstr ""

#: src/tab-switcher.md:30
msgid ""
"Press <kbd class=\"keybinding\">down\\|down</kbd> to move to the next tab in "
"the list"
msgstr ""

#: src/tab-switcher.md:31
msgid ""
"Press <kbd class=\"keybinding\">up\\|up</kbd> to move to the previous tab"
msgstr ""

#: src/tab-switcher.md:35
msgid ""
"Press <kbd class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-backspace\\|ctrl-backspace</kbd> to "
"close the currently selected tab"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:5
msgid ""
"Zed has built-in Git support that lets you manage version control without "
"leaving the editor. The Git Panel shows your working tree state, staging "
"area, and branch information. Changes you make on the command line are "
"reflected immediately in Zed."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:7
msgid ""
"For operations that Zed doesn't support natively, you can use the integrated "
"terminal."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:11
msgid ""
"The Git Panel shows the state of your working tree and Git's staging area."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:15
msgid ""
"In the panel you can see the state of your project at a glance: which "
"repository and branch are active, what files have changed and the current "
"staging state of each file."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:21
msgid ""
"Open the Settings Editor (`Cmd+,` on macOS, `Ctrl+,` on Linux/Windows) to "
"customize Git behavior. Settings are spread across two pages:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:23
msgid ""
"**Panels > Git Panel**: Panel position, tree vs flat view, status display "
"style"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:24
msgid "**Version Control**: Gutter indicators, inline blame, hunk styles"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:26
msgid "Moving the Git Panel"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:28
msgid ""
"By default, the Git Panel docks on the left. Go to **Panels > Git Panel** "
"and change **Git Panel Dock** to move it to the right or bottom."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:30
msgid "Switching to Tree View"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:32
msgid ""
"The Git Panel shows a flat list of changed files by default. To see files "
"organized by folder hierarchy instead, toggle **Tree View** in the panel's "
"context menu, or enable it in **Panels > Git Panel**."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:34
msgid "Inline Blame"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:36
msgid ""
"Zed shows Git blame information on the current line. To turn this off or add "
"a delay before it appears, go to **Version Control > Inline Git Blame**."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:38
msgid "Hiding the Gutter Indicators"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:40
msgid ""
"The colored bars in the gutter that show added, modified, and deleted lines "
"can be hidden. Go to **Version Control > Git Gutter** and set **Visibility** "
"to \"Hide\"."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:42
msgid "Commit Message Line Length"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:44
msgid ""
"Zed wraps commit messages at 72 characters (a Git convention). To change "
"this, search for \"Git Commit\" in Settings and adjust **Preferred Line "
"Length**."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:48
msgid ""
"You can see all of the changes captured by Git in Zed by opening the Project "
"Diff (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-g d\\|ctrl-g d</kbd>), accessible via "
"the <code class=\"hljs\">git: diff</code> action in the Command Palette or "
"the Git Panel."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:54
msgid "Word Diff Highlighting"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:56
msgid ""
"By default, Zed highlights changed words within modified lines to make it "
"easier to spot exactly what changed. To disable this globally, open the "
"Settings Editor and go to **Languages & Tools > Miscellaneous**, then turn "
"off **Word Diff Enabled**."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:58
msgid ""
"To disable word diff for specific languages only, add this to your settings."
"json:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:64
msgid "\"word_diff_enabled\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:70
msgid "Diff View Styles"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:72
msgid ""
"Zed displays diffs in two modes: **split** (side-by-side comparison) or "
"**unified** (inline changes). Split view is the default."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:74
msgid "Changing the diff view"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:76
msgid ""
"Open the Settings Editor (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-,\\|ctrl-,</kbd>) "
"and search for \"diff view style\". Select either **Split** or **Unified**."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:78
msgid "To change the default, add this to your `settings.json`:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:82
msgid "\"diff_view_style\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:82
msgid "\"unified\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:86
msgid ""
"See [Configuring Zed](./configuring-zed.md) for more about the Settings "
"Editor."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:88
msgid "Split vs unified"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:90
msgid ""
"**Split**: Shows the original and modified versions side by side. Useful for "
"comparing file structure or reviewing large changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:91
msgid ""
"**Unified**: Shows changes inline with additions and deletions in a single "
"view. Useful for focusing on specific line changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:93
msgid ""
"You can switch between modes at any time. Your preference applies to "
"[Project Diff](#project-diff), [File History](#file-history), and [Stash "
"Diff View](#stash-diff-view). These diff views function as [multibuffers](./"
"multibuffers.md), allowing you to edit multiple excerpts simultaneously."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:95
msgid "File History"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:97
msgid ""
"File History shows the commit history for an individual file. Each entry "
"displays the commit's author, timestamp, and message. Selecting a commit "
"opens a diff view filtered to show only the changes made to that file in "
"that commit."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:99
msgid "To view File History:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:101
msgid ""
"Right-click on a file in the Project Panel and select \"View File History\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:102
msgid "Right-click on a file in the Git Panel and select \"View File History\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:103
msgid "Right-click on an editor tab and select \"View File History\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:104
msgid "Use the Command Palette and search for \"file history\""
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:106
msgid "Fetch, Push, and Pull"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:110
msgid "Push Configuration"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:112
msgid ""
"Zed respects Git's push configuration. When pushing, Zed checks the "
"following in order:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:114
msgid "`pushRemote` configured for the current branch"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:115
msgid "`remote.pushDefault` in your Git config"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:116
msgid "The branch's tracking remote"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:118
msgid ""
"This matches Git's standard behavior, so if you've configured `pushRemote` "
"or `pushDefault` in your `.gitconfig` or via `git config`, Zed will use "
"those settings."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:120
msgid "Remotes"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:122
msgid ""
"When your repository has multiple remotes, Zed shows a remote selector in "
"the Git Panel. Click the remote button next to push/pull to choose which "
"remote to use for that operation."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:130
msgid ""
"In the Project Diff view, you can focus on each hunk and stage them "
"individually by clicking on the tab bar buttons or via the keybindings <code "
"class=\"hljs\">git: stage and next</code> (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-y\\|"
"alt-y</kbd>)."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:132
msgid ""
"Similarly, stage all hunks at the same time with the <code "
"class=\"hljs\">git: stage all</code> (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-ctrl-y\\|"
"ctrl-space</kbd>) keybinding and then immediately commit with <code "
"class=\"hljs\">git: commit</code> (<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-enter\\|"
"ctrl-enter</kbd>)."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:148
msgid ""
"The first one is available right at the bottom of the Git Panel. Hitting "
"<kbd class=\"keybinding\">cmd-enter\\|ctrl-enter</kbd> immediately commits "
"all of your staged changes."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:149
msgid ""
"The second is available via the action <code class=\"hljs\">git: expand "
"commit editor</code> or via hitting the <kbd class=\"keybinding\">shift-"
"escape\\|</kbd> while focused in the Git Panel commit textarea."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:162
msgid "Branch Management"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:164
msgid "Creating and Switching Branches"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:166
msgid ""
"Create a new branch using <code class=\"hljs\">git: branch</code> or switch "
"to an existing branch using <code class=\"hljs\">git: switch</code> or <code "
"class=\"hljs\">git: checkout branch</code>."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:168
msgid "Deleting Branches"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:170
msgid ""
"To delete a branch, open the branch switcher with <code class=\"hljs\">git: "
"switch</code>, find the branch you want to delete, and use the delete "
"option. Zed will confirm before deleting to prevent accidental data loss."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:172
msgid ""
"**Note:** You cannot delete the branch you currently have checked out. "
"Switch to a different branch first."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:174
msgid "Merge Conflicts"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:176
msgid ""
"When you encounter merge conflicts after a merge, rebase, or pull, Zed "
"highlights the conflicting regions in your files and displays resolution "
"buttons above each conflict."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:178
msgid "Viewing Conflicts"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:180
msgid ""
"Conflicting files appear in the Git Panel with a warning icon. You can also "
"see conflicts in the Project Diff view, where each conflict region is "
"highlighted:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:182
msgid "Changes from your current branch are highlighted in green"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:183
msgid "Changes from the incoming branch are highlighted in blue"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:185
msgid "Resolving Conflicts"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:187
msgid "Each conflict shows three buttons:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:189
msgid ""
"**Use \\[branch-name\\]**: Keep the changes from one branch (shows the "
"actual branch name, like \"main\")"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:190
msgid ""
"**Use \\[other-branch\\]**: Keep the changes from the other branch (like "
"\"feature-branch\")"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:191
msgid ""
"**Use Both**: Keep both sets of changes, with your branch's changes first"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:193
msgid ""
"Click a button to resolve that conflict. The conflict markers are removed "
"and replaced with your chosen content. After resolving all conflicts in a "
"file, stage it and commit to complete the merge."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:195
msgid ""
"**Tip:** For complex conflicts that need manual editing, you can edit the "
"file directly. Remove the conflict markers (`<<<<<<<`, `=======`, `>>>>>>>`) "
"and keep the content you want."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:207
msgid ""
"Zed provides a stash picker accessible via <code class=\"hljs\">git: view "
"stash</code> or from the Git Panel's overflow menu. From the stash picker, "
"you can:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:224
msgid ""
"To view a stash's contents, select it in the stash picker and press <kbd "
"class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-shift-v\\|ctrl-shift-v</kbd>. From the diff view, "
"you can use these keybindings:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:228
msgid "Apply stash"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:228
msgid "<kbd class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-space\\|ctrl-space</kbd>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:229
msgid "Pop stash (apply and remove)"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:229
msgid "<kbd class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-shift-space\\|ctrl-shift-space</kbd>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:230
msgid "Drop stash (remove without applying)"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:230
msgid ""
"<kbd class=\"keybinding\">ctrl-shift-backspace\\|ctrl-shift-backspace</kbd>"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:234
msgid ""
"Zed currently supports LLM-powered commit message generation. You can ask AI "
"to generate a commit message by focusing on the message editor within the "
"Git Panel and either clicking on the pencil icon in the bottom left, or "
"reaching for the <code class=\"hljs\">git: generate commit message</code> "
"(<kbd class=\"keybinding\">alt-tab\\|alt-l</kbd>) keybinding."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:237
msgid ""
"Note that you need to have an LLM provider configured either via your own "
"API keys or through Zed's hosted AI models. Visit [the AI configuration page]"
"(./ai/configuration.md) to learn how to do so."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:254
msgid ""
"To customize the format of generated commit messages, run <code "
"class=\"hljs\">agent: open rules library</code> and select the \"Commit "
"message\" rule on the left side. From there, you can modify the prompt to "
"match your desired format."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:259
msgid ""
"Any specific instructions for commit messages added to [Rules files](./ai/"
"rules.md) are also picked up by the model tasked with writing your commit "
"message."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:272
msgid "Self-Hosted Instances"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:274
msgid ""
"Zed automatically identifies Git hosting providers by checking for keywords "
"in your Git remote URL. For example, if your self-hosted URL contains "
"`gitlab`, `gitea`, or other recognized provider names, Zed will "
"automatically register that hosting provider without any configuration "
"needed."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:276
msgid ""
"However, if your self-hosted Git instance URL doesn't contain identifying "
"keywords, you can manually configure Zed to create clickable links to your "
"instance by adding a `git_hosting_providers` setting so commit hashes and "
"permalinks resolve to your domain:"
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:290
msgid ""
"The `provider` field specifies which type of hosting service you're using. "
"Supported `provider` values are `github`, `gitlab`, `bitbucket`, `gitea`, "
"`forgejo`, and `sourcehut`. The `name` is optional and used as a display "
"name for your instance, and `base_url` is the root URL of your self-hosted "
"server."
msgstr ""

#: src/git.md:292
msgid ""
"You can configure multiple custom providers if you work with several self-"
"hosted instances."
msgstr ""

